<<showCharacter "Lina" "SpeakingTired">>
Lina: Oh she just had bad luck with her previous classmates, they didn't really make her part of any of the groups. 
<<showCharacter "Lina" "ListeningTired">>
Mailman: Oh, that's too bad. She's a lovely girl.
<<showCharacter "Lina" "SpeakingTired">>
Lina: She felt like she was responsible for what was happening and started to overthink every interaction she had with any of the kids. She came home exhausted every day and her grades started to take a toll.
<<showCharacter "Lina" "ListeningTired">>
Mailman: I'm glad she changed schools.
<<showCharacter "Lina" "SpeakingTired">>
Lina: If you meet any kid that attends her new school and seems nice enough, please tell me and maybe I can organize a hangout for them to meet Sofie.
<<showCharacter "Lina" "ListeningTired">>
Mailman: Will do! I'm sure she'll have a wonderful group of classmates.
<<showCharacter "Lina" "SpeakingTired">>
Lina: I really hope so, she's been through enough.
===
title: AEnd1Day4
group: FamA && Day4
color: green
position: -1369,1521
---
<<showCharacter "Lina" "SpeakingTired">>
Lina: It's okay, I'm sure she'll meet amazing kids in this new school. She just needs to stop getting ahead of what's going to happen.
<<showCharacter "Lina" "ListeningTired">>
Mailman: She does?
<<showCharacter "Lina" "SpeakingTired">>
Lina: Yes, she prepares for all the negative outcomes possible, she says it's so she knows how to react, but I bet it's exhausting for her, she has enough already getting adjusted to new teachers and subjects.
<<showCharacter "Lina" "ListeningTired">>
Mailman: That does sound like a lot. I hope she meets the right kids. 
<<showCharacter "Lina" "SpeakingTired">>
Lina: Me too. Thank you for listening. 
<<showCharacter "Lina" "ListeningTired">>
Mailman: No worries, of you need any help count with me.
===

